      "findingCount": 1,
      "published": true,
      "jsonReport": "pr-334889-3e5d8f7d9fdf.json",
      "markdownReport": "pr-334889-3e5d8f7d9fdf.md",
      "publishedComments": [
        {
          "path": "src/vs/workbench/contrib/browserView/common/browserView.ts",
          "line": 113,
          "side": "RIGHT",
          "body": "**[Experimental performance review bot]**\n\n**Severity: medium**\n\nThe shared newest-first helper inserts every match at index zero, shifting the accumulated array for each matching browser on every recomputation.\n\nWhen an agent session accumulates many browser pages, each page load/navigation emits several label events; both pill surfaces can repeatedly perform quadratic array copying before updating the UI, delaying rendering and increasing GC pressure.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Append matching inputs with `push` during the map walk and call `views.reverse()` once afterward; this preserves newest-first ordering and restores O(n) construction.\n\n(Written by Copilot)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
